    section: "B", questionRef: "2025 OL Q10(c)(i)–(v)",
    stem: "Boron carbide (B₄C) is an extremely hard ceramic used in some padlocks. It is made by heating boron trioxide (B₂O₃) with carbon (C) in an electric furnace. In a reaction, 140 g of B₂O₃ was heated in the presence of excess carbon to give B₄C and carbon monoxide (CO) according to the following balanced chemical equation: 2B₂O₃ + 7C → B₄C + 6CO The relative molecular mass (Mr) of B₂O₃ is 70.",
