    id: "chem-2022-ol-q10-c-i", topicId: "chem-1-4", conceptId: "moles-from-mass",
    section: "B", questionRef: "2022 OL Q10(c)(i)",
    stem: "The NASA Perseverance Rover that landed on Mars in 2021 contained MOXIE, a small test unit designed to extract oxygen by electrolysis from the Martian atmosphere, which is mostly carbon dioxide, according to the following balanced equation. 2CO₂ → O₂ + 2CO In a test conducted in April 2021 on Mars, MOXIE produced 5.4 g of O₂ in one hour.",
    questionText: "How many moles of oxygen (O₂) are there in 5.4 g?",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed"}, totalMarks: 6,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "point", verbatim: "n = m ÷ Mr ⇒ 5.4 ÷ 32", marks: 3, contextNote: "The scheme prints m over Mr and 5.4 over 32 as fractions; ÷ stands for their bars.", openList: true },
    { id: "r-2", kind: "point", verbatim: "= 0.16875 moles O₂", marks: 3, openList: true },
    ],
