          "alt": "The marking scheme's own answer to 2025 OL Q2(d), as the State Examinations Commission printed it: two routes side by side. Left, by the titration formula: M × 18.4 over 2 equals 25 × 0.05 over 1, giving 0.13 - 0.14 M. Right, by moles: (0.05)(25) over 1000 = 0.00125 (moles per 25 cm³); 0.00125 × 2 = 0.0025; (0.0025)(1000) over 18 = 0.13 - 0.14 M; with the mark (5 + 2 + 2).",
          "attribution": "SEC Leaving Certificate Chemistry 2025 Ordinary Level — © State Examinations Commission",
